# Reference terminology: binding for translators and auditors, never a QA gate.
#
# Packets receive the entries whose `source` (or one of its `aliases`) occurs in their own
# units, exactly as approved terms are filtered, so appending entries for a new chapter
# changes only the audit context of the batches that mention them. Correcting an existing
# entry likewise resets only the batches it matches.
#
# Every entry is a `terms:` item with the same matching fields as approved.yaml:
#   source     the form to locate in the source text
#   aliases    other attested forms that also select the entry (e.g. derived compounds)
#   match      substring (default) | word | regex
#   scope      document (default) | page:N | a parent unit id
#   kind       a project-defined category shown as its own group in packets; default
#              `{{ default_reference_kind }}`. Suggested kinds:
#              proper-name  a name kept in source form (no target; note the generic noun rule)
#              sense        one word, several senses: list `targets` and the `rule` that decides
#   status     `reference-only` (default). `proposed` is inert; `approved` is refused here.
# Any other key (target, targets, rule, note, first_seen, ...) is passed to packets verbatim.
#
# Examples (delete when adding real entries):
#   - kind: proper-name
#     source: Hölder
#     aliases: [Hölder inequality, Hölder continuous]
#     note: keep the name in source form; translate the generic noun
#   - kind: sense
#     source: partition
#     targets: [划分, 配分函数]
#     rule: a partition of a set is 划分; `partition function` is 配分函数
terms: []
